{"term":"scout","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1d1a2ca5776ff98750","definition":"A person sent out to gather and bring back information; especially, one employed in war to gain information about the enemy and ground.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["espial","espy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad569d83bf7f05dea6","definition":"An act of scouting or reconnoitering.","example":"while the rat is on the scout","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:97bc2032df87378506","definition":"A member of any number of youth organizations belonging to the international scout movement, such as the Boy Scouts of America or Girl Scouts of the United States.","example":"At the crack of dawn on Wednesday four different groups of scouts will climb the highest peaks in England, Scotland, Northern Ireland and Wales to light flames and officially mark the start of the Paralympic torch relay.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cfe0eccd33e916655b","definition":"A person who assesses or recruits others; especially, one who identifies promising talent on behalf of a sports team.","example":"We have met twice this year and, during our first interview, Mata spoke evocatively when remembering how, having joined Real Oviedo aged 10 in 1998, he was given a previously unimaginable opportunity. Mata sat in a car park in 2003, when he was 14, and watched his father talking to a Real Madrid scout.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25f0ff9d1a56bb87a6","definition":"A person employed to monitor rivals' activities in the petroleum industry.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6402da6a59cc40c3e6","definition":"A housekeeper or domestic cleaner, generally female, employed by one of the constituent colleges of Oxford University to clean rooms; generally equivalent to a modern bedder at Cambridge University.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"modern","register":"modern","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:775768d7e8e4740b5e","definition":"A domestic servant, generally male, who would attend (usually several) students in a variety of ways, including cleaning; generally equivalent to a gyp at Cambridge University or a skip at Trinity College, Dublin.","example":"He has also been good enough to recommend to me many tradesmen who are ready to supply these articles in any quantities; each of whom has been here already a dozen times, cap in hand, and vowing that it is quite immaterial when I pay—which is very kind of them; but, with the highest respect for friend Perkins (my scout) and his obliging friends, I shall make some enquiries before \"letting in\" with any of them.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3768fbb9bec6f7ddb8","definition":"A fielder in a game for practice.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f9f19584064623ceb1","definition":"A fighter aircraft.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, historical","register":"UK, historical","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8ffd12384d621bf9af","definition":"A preliminary image that allows the technician to make adjustments before the actual diagnostic images.","example":"A scout topogram is initially performed during continuous table motion, generating an anatomic overview image similar to a conventional radiograph at the locked projection.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5488548b426cea6051","definition":"A term of address for a man or boy.","example":"\"Listen, old scout,\" Mr. Osborn said solemnly, \"you think New York is heartless, but that's not what it is.\"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2e6eabe480b7792918","definition":"To explore a wide terrain, as if on a search.","example":"An hundred horeſmen of my companie\nScowting abroad vpon theſe champion plaines,\nHaue view’d the army of the Scythians,\nWhich make report it far exceeds the Kings.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["survey","reconnoiter"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout","scout about","scout around","scout out","scout round","scout up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d40fb4a24feee935ea","definition":"To observe, watch, or look for, as a scout; to follow for the purpose of observation, as a scout.","example":"Take more men, and scout him round.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout","scout about","scout around","scout out","scout round","scout up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d49a7a713f4f15ccf3","definition":"To reject with contempt.","example":"to scout an idea or an apology","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["boy scout","go on the scout","scout balloon","scout car","scoutess","Scout Green","scouthouse","scoutmaster","Scout Official for a Day","scout team","talent scout","scout about","s